<section id="backupsView" class="view-panel hidden" aria-labelledby="backupsTitle">
    <div class="backup-page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR FILES, WITH A SECOND HOME</p><h1 id="backupsTitle">Backups</h1><p>Make a copy when you need one. Keep it somewhere safe.</p></div><span class="backup-heading-tag"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-lock"/></svg> Manual exports only</span></div>
    <div id="backupStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="backup-status"></div>
    <article class="backup-card">
        <header class="backup-card-header"><div><h2>Manual backup</h2><p>Three steps. You choose when to make a copy.</p></div><span class="backup-badge">SQL + encrypted file ZIP</span></header>
        <div class="backup-steps">
            <section><span class="backup-step-number">1</span><h3>Download your backup files</h3><p>Save the database as SQL and your new or changed uploads as an encrypted ZIP.</p><button id="downloadSqlBackup" class="button backup-action" type="button" disabled><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-download"/></svg><span>Download SQL</span></button><p class="backup-hint">Your download starts when the export is ready.</p><button id="downloadZipBackup" class="backup-secondary backup-action" type="button" disabled><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-download"/></svg><span>Download encrypted file ZIP</span></button><p id="backupFileSummary" class="backup-hint">Loading file totals…</p><p id="backupAvailability" class="backup-hint"></p></section>
            <section><span class="backup-step-number">2</span><h3>Open your backup folder</h3><p>Open Google Drive using an account that can access your backup folder.</p><a id="backupDriveFolder" class="backup-secondary backup-drive-link" href="https://drive.google.com/drive/my-drive" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Google Drive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p id="backupDriveHint" class="backup-hint">Opens in a new tab.</p></section>
            <section><span class="backup-step-number">3</span><h3>Upload the SQL and ZIP files</h3><p>In Drive, choose <strong>New → File upload</strong> and select the files you just downloaded. Keep the SQL and all required incremental ZIPs together.</p><div class="backup-reminder">Wait for Google Drive to show that the upload has finished.</div></section>
        </div>
        <div class="backup-included"><h3>What is included?</h3><p><strong>SQL:</strong> database records, including accounts, buckets, object metadata, access-token records, and backup history. SQL is not encrypted; keep it in a restricted folder.</p><p><strong>Encrypted ZIP:</strong> new or changed registered uploads, a recovery manifest, and checksums. The first export includes existing files; later exports are incremental. Keep every ZIP needed for recovery.</p><p>Open the encrypted ZIP with 7-Zip or WinRAR, using the password configured by your administrator. Windows Extract all does not support this encryption. The password is never shown here. Download both files close together and avoid changing uploads while exports are being prepared.</p><p>Drive uploads are manual. This app does not upload files, confirm off-site copies, or run scheduled backups. Preparing a large ZIP can take time and requires temporary server disk space.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article class="backup-card backup-history"><header class="backup-card-header"><div><h2>Recent backup exports</h2><p>Prepared downloads only. This list does not confirm a file was saved to Drive.</p></div><button id="refreshBackups" class="backup-secondary" type="button">Refresh list</button></header><div class="backup-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Prepared</th><th>Backup file</th><th>Type</th><th>Size</th><th>Administrator</th><th aria-label="Download again"></th></tr></thead><tbody id="backupExportList"><tr><td colspan="6">Loading exports…</td></tr></tbody></table></div></article>
</section>
